    "https://capital.applicantpro.com/jobs/3982341": {
      "title": "Chemistry and Biochemistry Instructors (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Chemistry and Biochemistry Instructors (Part-Time). Capital University. Capital University seeks passionate science educators with experience in general chemistry and organic chemistry for part-time instructor positions in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry in Summer and Fall 2026. For Summer 2026, successful candidates should be able to teach both lecture and laboratory in general chemistry (for STEM majors) and/or organic chemistry. Students in these courses will be chemistry, biochemistry, biology, environmental science, and exercise science majors, with potentially some other majors who are planning for professional school in health-related fields. For Fall 2026, successful candidates should be able to teach both lecture and laboratory in general chemistry for STEM majors (Chemical Principles) and/or general, organic, and biological chemistry to primarily nursing majors (GOB Chemistry). Students in these courses will be chemistry, biochemistry, biology, environmental science, exercise science, and nursing majors. There could be opportunities to teach other introductory and upper-level courses as well as University Signature Learning program courses in the sciences during the academic year as well. Qualified candidates will have a Ph.D. at the time of appointment or related experiences. Applicants must demonstrate evidence of excellence in teaching and preference will be given to applicants that incorporate evidence-based teaching practices in their classrooms. Interested candidates should send 1) cover letter and 2) a curriculum vitae. Please upload all requested documents to the drop box on the application. Applications for this position should be submitted through the Capital University website : https://capital.applicantpro.com/jobs/ For specific questions, contact us Dr. Tracey Murray at tmurray2@capital.edu The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The positions for summer term begin in May 2026 and fall term in August 2026. Capital University is currently unable to sponsor employment Visas or consider candidates who will require Visa sponsorship. For more information on Capital University, visit our website at www.capital.edu . Capital University is an equal opportunity employer. Capital University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, religion, sex, gender, age, disability, veteran status, or other characteristics protected by the law."
    },
    "https://capital.applicantpro.com/jobs/4152814": {
      "title": "Director of Trinity Lutheran Seminary Advancement",
      "description": "Director of Trinity Lutheran Seminary Advancement. Capital University. Position Summary The Advancement Officer advances the philanthropic mission of Trinity Lutheran Seminary (TLS) and Capital University by cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding donors while strengthening alumni engagement and fostering lifelong relationships with Trinity Lutheran Seminary alumni, dual Capital-Trinity alumni, and friends of the Seminary. They will build and manage a portfolio of major gift and planned gift prospects, alumni, foundations, congregations, and other philanthropic partners across Columbus and throughout the country to secure financial support for scholarships, academic initiatives, campus priorities, and other strategic Seminary and University initiatives. The position serves as the primary liaison to Trinity Lutheran Seminary alumni, creating meaningful opportunities for engagement, volunteerism, and philanthropy that strengthen lifelong connections to the institution. Working collaboratively as a member of the Capital University Advancement team, the Director partners with colleagues across Advancement, Seminary leadership, faculty, and volunteers to advance fundraising priorities and deepen constituent engagement. The position reports directly to the Senior Director of Regional Development and Campaign Advisor, with a dotted-line reporting relationship to the Dean of Trinity Lutheran Seminary. Key Responsibilities · Build and manage a portfolio of approximately 100+ high-capacity donors and prospects and actively cultivate and solicit gifts. Accordingly, this position requires frequent travel in the field regionally and throughout the U.S. · Raise Philanthropic Giving: Cultivate, solicit, and close five- and six-figure gifts. · Collaboration: Partner with the university advancement team on major campaigns including annual giving programs for TLS, alumni gatherings, and philanthropic campaign projects. · Travel Nationwide: Visit donors face-to-face to share the seminary's mission. · Engage Lutheran Networks: Steward the Seminary's connections with synods, pastors, and ecclesial/nonprofit foundations for philanthropic purposes. In this responsibility, work closely with the Dean of the Seminary, the University Pastor, and the Director of Contextual Education and Community Life. · Ongoing Stewardship of Assessment: Perform intentional follow-up with donors and alumni after events to nurture relationships, future philanthropic opportunities, and stewardship of current endowed funds. · Active TLS Community Member: Participate regularly and fully in weekly TLS community events, including chapel, lunches, lecture series, faculty and staff meetings, and retreats, etc. · Alumni Engagement: Steward the relationships between alumni and the seminary and broader university, including hosting events for the Seminary. Initial Two-Year Metrics & Goals · Donor Visits: Conduct 100 to 120 face-to-face donor visits annually (use the Dean and Team) (combination of individuals and ecclesial/philanthropic foundations). · Gift Solicitations: Submit 20 to 30 formal asks (using the Dean and Trinity Lutheran Seminary Team). · Fundraising Target: Meet or exceed annual solicitation goals (submitted and realized) set by leadership based on annual projects, institutional priorities, and campaign efforts. · Portfolio Qualification: Qualify 30 new prospects during the first two years for continued portfolio renewal and growth. · Database Management: Log all donor actions accurately into the CRM, hitting goals for visits, proposals, and engagement. · Regularly attend various Trinity Lutheran Seminary events with an emphasis on strategically inviting and cultivating relationships with assigned constituents. Qualifications · This position requires personal attendance at Trinity Lutheran Seminary's campus in Bexley, OH. · Experience: Three to five years in professional fundraising or church advancement. · Demonstrated ability to understand the needs and interests of donors to develop and strengthen relationships within the Seminary and University. · Excellent written and verbal communication, grammar and spelling skills, and telephone etiquette. · Highly relational with demonstrated ability to interact with donors and prospects of all ages. Able to work with many different people and handle a variety of tasks, all with a good sense of humor. · Good organizational and time management skills. The ability to work independently and be a self-starter while engaging in multiple tasks. · Dependability, integrity, and ability to receive and implement suggestions from supervisors. · Education: Bachelor's degree required, as well as an MDiv or equivalent. · Skills: Proficiency in CRM systems, preferably in Blackbaud NXT and FPM software. · Faith Commitment: Proficiency in ELCA and Lutheranism required. · Must be able and willing to travel regionally and throughout the U.S. and work before or after work hours and over the weekends. Capital University is currently unable to sponsor employment Visas or consider candidates who will require Visa sponsorship. For more information on Capital University, visit our website at www.capital.edu. The salary range for this role is between $70 - $90k, commensurate with experience. Capital University offers a rich benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, retirement, family education benefits, short-term and long-term disability, life insurance and free parking. Capital University is an equal opportunity employer. Capital University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, religion, sex, gender, age, disability, veteran status, or other characteristics protected by the law."
    },
    "https://capital.applicantpro.com/jobs/4208458": {
      "title": "Electrician",
      "description": "Electrician. Capital University. Under the supervision of the Director of Facilities Management, installs, maintains, and repairs electrical wiring systems, fixtures, controls, and equipment to maintain and improve Capital University facilities. Responsibilities: Installs, inspects, and tests electrical lighting, signal, communication and power circuits and equipment, both residential and commercial applications. Isolates and repairs in wiring, switches, motors, motor controls, boiler / chiller systems, and other electrical equipment. Replaces faulty switches, sockets, plugs, fuses, insulators, lighting, and other simple elements of electrical systems, fixtures, and appliances. Renews circuits either by isolating and cutting out defective wiring and replacing it with new wiring, or by splicing ends of broken wires. Responsible for estimating and running additional electrical circuits from panels to point of use. Replaces defective equipment while following LOTO policy, to restore equipment and systems. As required, estimate materials needed and record time and materials expended on each work order. Must be able to respond to emergencies as applicable and or willing to work overtime as needed on emergent repairs. Assist with managing and or assisting external contractors on larger electrical projects. Qualifications: Knowledge and experience in electrical maintenance, repair, and installation, and associated hand and power tools and equipment. Minimum 5 years of experience in commercial / residential and service. Must have working knowledge and understanding of current NEC. Motor Vehicle operator's license and dependable transportation required. Ability to read blueprints and follow technical instructions. Ability to perform tasks in low, high, and tight spaces such as closets, windows, crawl spaces under floors and above ceilings, stairwells, equipment rooms, building exteriors, and roofs. Ability to handle exposure: to dirt, dust, and grease, electricity, climatic weather, various chemicals such as drain cleaners, mastics, glues, paint, loud equipment noises with multiple moving parts. Physical Requirements: ability to lift 50 lbs. on a regular basis. For more information on Capital University, visit our website at www.capital.edu. Capital University offers a rich benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, retirement, family education benefits, short-term and long-term disability, life insurance and free parking. Capital University is an equal opportunity employer. Capital University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, religion, sex, gender, age, disability, veteran status, or other characteristics protected by the law. Capital University is currently unable to sponsor employment Visas or consider candidates who will require Visa sponsorship."
    },
    "https://capital.applicantpro.com/jobs/3910429": {
      "title": "ESL Instructors (Part-Time)",
      "description": "ESL Instructors (Part-Time) - Columbus, OH - Capital University Jobs Jobs Login Back to all jobs ESL Instructors (Part-Time) 1 College and Main, Columbus, OH 43209, US Part Time Email Me Similar Jobs Email Me This Job The Intensive English Program at Capital University is seeking to hire Adjunct ESL instructors. Contracts are issued on a semester-by-semester basis. The ESL Program provides international students with supportive and vigorous language instruction that will lead to preparation for a student's next academic journey. Instructional delivery is in-person, Monday -Thursday, and classes meet from 8:30 am – 2:30 pm. Depending on enrollment, teaching assignments may be for 1-3 classes. Requirements: Master's degree in TESOL or a closely-related field (English, Linguistics, Education). Minimum one to three years of teaching academic reading, writing, listening and speaking in an Intensive English Program (IEP) or English for Academic Purpose (EAP) program. Creative classroom presence with an ability to teach from basic to advanced students. Effective written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills and attention to detail. Effective use of technology in the classroom. Ability to work effectively and collaboratively with colleagues. Assist with end of semester testing, grading, and other tasks. Application Process: Interested candidates should submit 1) Cover letter that outlines the applicant's IEP/ESL experience as well as an educational philosophy to teaching international students of varied backgrounds, 2) a current CV , 3) Unofficial/copies of MA transcript, 4) names of three professional references (w/phone number & email address). Please upload all documents listed above to the drop box, when asked to upload resume on application. Capital University is currently unable to sponsor employment Visas or consider candidates who will require Visa sponsorship. For more information on Capital University, visit our website at www.capital.edu . Capital University is an equal opportunity employer. Capital University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, religion, sex, gender, age, disability, veteran status, or other characteristics protected by the law. Apply now How would you like to verify your identity? Continue with phone Verify with a one-time text code Continue with email Verify with a one-time code Powered by iSolved Talent Acquisition Sign Up For Job Alerts! Name You must type a name. Email You must type a valid email. Location (city, state or zip code) You must select a location. Accept Terms of Service I agree to the terms of service and privacy policy. You must accept the terms of service and privacy policy. Send Me Jobs Would you like Refer.io to send you similar jobs from other employers? Yes, daily! Yes, weekly! No, thanks. Please type the job title you are interested in: Job title You must type a job title. We'll send some jobs to you in the next 30 minutes. If you don't see them, check your spam folder. Next Resume Input Select file Resume File You must select a file. Upload Resume upload later Thank you for subscribing to receive job alerts. You should start receiving emails in the next week. Your file is uploading. Please wait a few seconds. Enter your phone number if you'd like to receive job alerts for in via text message. Phone number You must type a phone number. Please indicate if you agree to Refer.io's Subscriber Communication Policy . Please indicate if you agree to Refer.io's Subscriber Communication Policy. Select an option Yes, I agree to be contacted by text messages No, I do not agree to receive text messages You must agree to our Subscriber Communication Policy in order to receive text messages from Refer.io. Yes, why not? Not now Refer.io can assist in your job search. Please answer the following questions to amplify your search results. Education status Education status In School Graduated Never Attended Partially completed You must select an education status answer. Work status Work status Currently employed Out of work Temporary job You must select a work status answer. Job search status Job search status Actively looking for a job Passively looking for a job Not looking for a job You must select a job search status answer. Seeking for Employment goal Similar Job to What I Do Now Progress to a Higher Job in the Same Field Jump to a New Field of Work You must select a seeking status answer. Job type Job type Full Time Part Time From Home You must select a job type answer. Next powered by Refer.io Refer.io Share This Job Hiring Software Maintained by isolved Talent Acquisition - © 2026 Refresh Search the FAQ here Go Common Job Questions"
